n\n| HLR | Priority | Requirement | Epic | Notes |\n|-----|----------|-------------|------|-------|\n| HLR-1 | P0 | Administrators can view per-project GPU-hour consumption reports over selectable time ranges, computed from metering data | RHAISTRAT-9018-E002, RHAISTRAT-9018-E003 | Split by architectural sub-system (Rule 2): E002 computes and serves the reports (server side), E003 renders them in the admin view (web UI). Each half is necessary for the HLR. |\n| HLR-2 | P1 | Reports exportable as CSV and retrieved via a stable API for finance tooling | RHAISTRAT-9018-E002 (bundled) | Bundled with the P0 work: the CSV export and stable API serialize the same per-project GPU-hour aggregates over the same report data model the P0 reporting service computes — they share the data structure and API endpoint surface, so a split would double-touch the same files and build the same surface twice; not separately schedulable. |\n| HLR-3 | P1 | Dashboard admin view shows current-month consumption against each project's Kueue quota | RHAISTRAT-9018-E003 (bundled) | Bundled with the P0 work: the quota comparison renders in the same admin report view and against the same report data as the P0 consumption report (HLR-1) — it shares the UI surface, so a split would build the same view twice; not separately schedulable. The quota figures themselves are served by the reporting data service as supporting data. |\n| HLR-4 | P2 | Documentation covers report semantics (what counts as a GPU-hour) and export integration | RHAISTRAT-9018-E004 | docs-authoring epic, blocked by all Implementation epics per Rule 11. |\n\nAll four HLRs are covered; none orphaned.\n\n## Health Warnings\n\n- **Missing strategy sections** (non-blocking): no Impacted Teams table, no\n  Dependencies table, no Given/When/Then acceptance criteria, no NFRs, no\n  size/effort estimate. Owner teams were derived from architecture context, and\n  epic acceptance criteria were derived from the HLRs and problem statement.\n  Worth confirming team ownership — in particular the docs epic's owner — with\n  the strategy author.\n- **External timing risk** (the strategy's open question): the metering data\n  schema finalizes only when RHAISTRAT-9990 lands. That timing is externally\n  controlled and is therefore recorded here and in the epic risk notes, never as\n  an acceptance criterion. It is mitigated structurally: the contract-validation\n  investigation runs first and downstream epics carry a `rewrite` gate with a\n  fallback (isolation layer over the metering output).\n- **Epic size**: the strategy provides no effort estimate; all epics are scoped\n  within the epic-size guideline (one investigation, one server-side service,\n  one admin view, one documentation topic set — each a single sub-system and\n  work-product type).\n- **Priority consistency**: no inversions detected. Both reporting epics carry\n  HLR-1 (P0); the investigation blocks all P0 work so it is P0 by inheritance;\n  the docs epic takes P1 from the strategy's `Major` priority per the\n  docs-authoring exception.\n\n## Tiered Delivery\n\nThe external dependency (the metering data delivered by RHAISTRAT-9990, with\nuncertain timing) gates all user-facing value: no administrator-visible report\ncan ship without the metering data, so there is no user-facing Tier 1.\n\n- **Tier 1 (starts immediately — risk-reduction)**: the contract-validation\n  investigation. It reduces the external-timing risk by pinning down the\n  consumption contract, its stability classification, and the\n  direct-vs-isolation-layer decision before implementation effort is committed.\n- **Tier 2 (gated)**: the reporting data service, the admin view, and the\n  documentation — all blocked directly or transitively on the contract\n  resolution. Per Rule 21, the in-flight metering strategy is modeled as a\n  precondition with tiered delivery, not as an epic in this decomposition (the\n  metering team resolves it; this strategy must not re-implement collection).\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":46702,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8722bc4b010886fd","agent_id":"aa1e69f47a3efe2ba","session_id":"f1063ad1-f88e-4f24-95c5-f48c7743c72b","uuid":"72759249-5d81-4b83-90fc-79ed0ebdfb9e","timestamp":"2026-10-26T10:22:27.488Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9018"}
