{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-c223e73b-c4f7-47e6-80d8-28646035bf5b","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-b3026bf6b4eac838","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9018-jmt_40mr/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9018-E001.md","content":"# Validate the GPU usage metering data contract for chargeback reporting\n\n## Description\n\nThis investigation resolves the strategy's open question — the GPU usage metering data schema is owned by the in-flight GPU usage metering strategy (RHAISTRAT-9990) and is not final until that strategy lands — by pinning down the consumption contract that GPU chargeback reporting builds against, before implementation effort is committed. It produces a documented, validated contract and a recorded consumption decision that the reporting implementation work is gated on.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Document the metering data contract as currently defined by the in-flight GPU usage metering work: the data schema (fields, per-project attribution keys, time semantics), the access mechanism by which reporting will read the data, and the definition of a billable GPU-hour as delivered by the metering output.\n- Classify the contract's stability and finalization path together with the metering strategy's owners: what is settled, what is still in flux, and the expected timeline.\n- Decide and record the consumption approach: build the reporting layer directly against the contract, or through an isolation layer that maps the metering output to the report data model so later schema changes stay contained.\n- Validate the reporting requirements (per-project GPU-hour reports over selectable time ranges, CSV export via a stable API, current-month consumption against Kueue quota) against the contract and record any deltas or constraints they impose.\n- Record the Kueue quota data source (the platform queueing stack's ClusterQueue/LocalQueue quota model) that the quota comparison will read, and confirm it is available independently of the metering work.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- The metering data contract (schema, access mechanism, GPU-hour semantics, per-project attribution) is documented, with each element classified as settled or in flux and its finalization path recorded.\n- A consumption decision is recorded — direct consumption vs. isolation layer — with rationale and a fallback for the case where the contract changes after reporting work starts.\n- Each reporting requirement is checked against the contract and the outcome (feasible as stated vs. needs adjustment) is recorded, so downstream scope is confirmed or rewritten rather than assumed.\n- The Kueue quota data source for the current-month comparison is identified and confirmed readable independently of the metering data.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-1 (P0): validates that per-project GPU-hour consumption reports over selectable time ranges can be computed from the metering data, and determines the consumption approach.\n- HLR-2 (P1): confirms the data basis for CSV export and the stable API for finance tooling.\n- HLR-3 (P1): confirms the Kueue quota data source for the current-month comparison.\n\n## Risks / Notes\n\n- The contract's finalization is externally controlled by the metering strategy's schedule. This investigation resolves what can be known now and structures the residual risk; it cannot force finality. The external timing risk itself is recorded in the decomposition summary's Health Warnings.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":49621,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8722bc4b010886fd","agent_id":"aa1e69f47a3efe2ba","session_id":"f1063ad1-f88e-4f24-95c5-f48c7743c72b","uuid":"ada8324f-aecd-4e76-b29b-b09026680017","timestamp":"2026-10-26T10:22:42.872Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decomp