{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-d5f0f109-a66f-4855-93b8-580a4b5283b8","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-bfdd71da656ecafa","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9018-jmt_40mr/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9018-E002.md","content":"# Per-project GPU-hour report data service with CSV export and stable API\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic delivers the server-side GPU chargeback reporting capability of the Dashboard: computation of per-project GPU-hour consumption reports over selectable time ranges from the metering data delivered by the GPU usage metering work, exposed through a stable API for the administrator-facing view and for finance tooling, with CSV export. It consumes the metering data as validated by the metering data contract investigation and must not re-implement usage collection.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Compute per-project GPU-hour consumption aggregates over caller-selectable time ranges from the metering data (no re-implementation of the collection pipeline, which is owned by the GPU usage metering work).\n- Expose the report data through a stable API suitable for finance tooling retrieval.\n- Provide CSV export of the reports.\n- Serve per-project Kueue quota figures (from the platform queueing stack's ClusterQueue/LocalQueue quota model) alongside consumption so the administrator view can render the current-month comparison.\n- Follow the consumption approach decided by the metering data contract investigation (direct consumption of the contract, or an isolation layer mapping the metering output to the report data model).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Given metering data for a sample period, the report API returns per-project GPU-hour consumption for caller-selected time ranges that reconciles with the underlying metering data for that period.\n- Reports are exportable as CSV and retrievable via the documented stable API.\n- 