{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bc40a38a8952c3cd","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9018-E001\n3\ttitle: Validate the GPU usage metering data contract for chargeback reporting\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9018\n5\tcomponent: Dashboard\n6\tteam: RHOAI Dashboard\n7\ttype: Investigation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tinvestigation_signals:\n10\t  question_specificity: 1\n11\t  source_accessibility: 0\n12\t  local_runnability: 0\n13\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: -1\n14\t  human_judgment_required: -1\n15\timplementation_type: null\n16\tdependencies: []\n17\tai_signals: null\n18\tai_implementability: Low\n19\tai_implementability_score: -1\n20\tjira_key: null\n21\tbranch: null\n22\tgated_by: null\n23\tgate_failure_impact: null\n24\t---\n25\t# Validate the GPU usage metering data contract for chargeback reporting\n26\t\n27\t## Description\n28\t\n29\tThis investigation resolves the strategy's open question — the GPU usage metering data schema is owned by the in-flight GPU usage metering strategy (RHAISTRAT-9990) and is not final until that strategy lands — by pinning down the consumption contract that GPU chargeback reporting builds against, before implementation effort is committed. It produces a documented, validated contract and a recorded consumption decision that the reporting implementation work is gated on.\n30\t\n31\t## Scope\n32\t\n33\t- Document the metering data contract as currently defined by the in-flight GPU usage metering work: the data schema (fields, per-project attribution keys, time semantics), the access mechanism by which reporting will read the data, and the definition of a billable GPU-hour as delivered by the metering output.\n34\t- Classify the contract's stability and finalization path together with the metering strategy's owners: what is settled, what is still in flux, and the expected timeline.\n35\t- Decide and record the consumption approach: build the reporting layer directly against the contract, or through an isolation layer that maps the metering output to the report data model so later schema changes stay contained.\n36\t- Validate the reporting requirements (per-project GPU-hour reports over selectable time ranges, CSV export via a stable API, current-month consumption against Kueue quota) against the contract and record any deltas or constraints they impose.\n37\t- Record the Kueue quota data source (the platform queueing stack's ClusterQueue/LocalQueue quota model) that the quota comparison will read, and confirm it is available independently of the metering work.\n38\t\n39\t## Acceptance Criteria\n40\t\n41\t- The metering data contract (schema, access mechanism, GPU-hour semantics, per-project attribution) is documented, with each element classified as settled or in flux and its finalization path recorded.\n42\t- A consumption decision is recorded — direct consumption vs. isolation layer — with rationale and a fallback for the case where the contract changes after reporting work starts.\n43\t- Each reporting requirement is checked against the contract and the outcome (feasible as stated vs. needs adjustment) is recorded, so downstream scope is confirmed or rewritten rather than assumed.\n44\t- The Kueue quota data source for the current-month comparison is identified and confirmed readable independently of the metering data.\n45\t\n46\t## HLR Traceability\n47\t\n48\t- HLR-1 (P0): validates that per-project GPU-hour consumption reports over selectable time ranges can be computed from the metering data, and determines the consumption approach.\n49\t- HLR-2 (P1): confirms the data basis for CSV export and the stable API for finance tooling.\n50\t- HLR-3 (P1): confirms the Kueue quota data source for the current-month comparison.\n51\t\n52\t## Risks / Notes\n53\t\n54\t- The contract's finalization is externally controlled by the metering strategy's schedule. This investigation resolves what can be known now and structures the residual risk; it cannot force finality. The external timing risk itself is recorded in the decomposition summary's Health Warnings.\n55\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b92ef38b605fc8c9","agent_id":"a5bb3e126258997a9","session_id":"f1063ad1-f88e-4f24-95c5-f48c7743c72b","uuid":"b9822d6d-3847-49c8-a588-813211acdfa5","timestamp":"2026-10-26T10:25:08.666Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-bc40a38a8952c3cd","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9018 decomposition"}
