ta (no re-implementation of the collection pipeline, which is owned by the GPU usage metering work).\n44\t- Expose the report data through a stable API suitable for finance tooling retrieval.\n45\t- Provide CSV export of the reports.\n46\t- Serve per-project Kueue quota figures (from the platform queueing stack's ClusterQueue/LocalQueue quota model) alongside consumption so the administrator view can render the current-month comparison.\n47\t- Follow the consumption approach decided by the metering data contract investigation (direct consumption of the contract, or an isolation layer mapping the metering output to the report data model).\n48\t\n49\t## Acceptance Criteria\n50\t\n51\t- Given metering data for a sample period, the report API returns per-project GPU-hour consumption for caller-selected time ranges that reconciles with the underlying metering data for that period.\n52\t- Reports are exportable as CSV and retrievable via the documented stable API.\n53\t- Usage collection is not re-implemented: all consumption figures are computed from the metering data delivered by the GPU usage metering work.\n54\t- Per-project Kueue quota figures served for the administrator view reconcile with the platform queueing stack's quota model (ClusterQueue/LocalQueue) as exposed in the platform.\n55\t\n56\t## HLR Traceability\n57\t\n58\t- HLR-1 (P0): per-project GPU-hour consumption reports over selectable time ranges, computed from the metering data — server-side computation and serving.\n59\t- HLR-2 (P1): CSV export and stable API for finance tooling — bundled here because it serializes the same report data model the P0 computation produces.\n60\t- HLR-3 (P1): serving of per-project Kueue quota figures as supporting data for the administrator view's current-month comparison.\n61\t\n62\t## Risks / Notes\n63\t\n64\t- Externally-controlled timing: the metering data schema finalizes only when the in-flight GPU usage metering strategy lands. Per the validated contract, consume via direct binding or an isolation layer so schema drift stays contained; if the contract materially changes, the consumption layer of this epic is rewritten rather than the whole reporting surface.\n65\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b92ef38b605fc8c9","agent_id":"a5bb3e126258997a9","session_id":"f1063ad1-f88e-4f24-95c5-f48c7743c72b","uuid":"efb981a4-171d-4933-b153-9c290bc5ce2d","timestamp":"2026-10-26T10:25:09.343Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a0364449eeae8ded","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9018 decomposition"}
