{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-961ff1cb10177989","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tstrat_id: RHAISTRAT-9018\n3\tscore: 14\n4\tpass: true\n5\trecommendation: accept\n6\tissues: []\n7\terror: null\n8\t---\n9\t## Review Summary\n10\t\n11\tScore: 14/14 — pass\n12\tRecommendation: accept\n13\t\n14\tContract validator: OK (all mechanical checks passed — body sections, canonical\n15\tcomponent names, Rule 11 docs-last coverage, priority inheritance, no\n16\tparallel-forbidden edges, no kept size overages, bundled HLRs flagged in the\n17\tmatrix rows).\n18\t\n19\tTriage consistency: `triage: null` (full decomposition) with 4 epics —\n20\tconsistent; multi-epic output is expected.\n21\t\n22\t### 1. HLR Coverage (2/2)\n23\t\n24\tAll four HLRs map to epics and the traceability matrix is complete:\n25\t\n26\t- HLR-1 (P0) → E002 (server-side computation/serving) + E003 (admin view\n27\t  rendering), split by architectural sub-system — each half is necessary.\n28\t- HLR-2 (P1) → E002, bundled with the `bundled` flag and rationale in the\n29\t  matrix row. The bundling judgment is sound: CSV export and the stable API\n30\t  serialize the same per-project GPU-hour aggregates over the same report data\n31\t  model the P0 service computes — a thin increment on the same surface, not a\n32\t  separately schedulable feature.\n33\t- HLR-3 (P1) → E003, bundled with rationale (same admin view, same report\n34\t  data). Correct shape per the same reasoning.\n35\t- HLR-4 (P2) → E004.\n36\t\n37\tPriority inheritance is correct: E001 (Investigation) blocks all P0 work and\n38\tis P0; E002/E003 carry HLR-1 (P0); E004 is `docs-authoring` and takes P1 from\n39\tthe strategy's `Major` priority per the docs-authoring exception — its Rule 11\n40\tdependencies on P0 implementations are not flagged, correctly. No priority\n41\tcollapse with deferrable features: both P1 bundlings are same-surface\n42\tincrements with recorded rationale, not independently plannable features.\n43\t\n44\t### 2. DAG Coherence (2/2)\n45\t\n46\tDAG: E001→E002, E001→E003, E002→E003, E002→E004, E003→E004. Verified edge by\n47\tedge:\n48\t\n49\t- E001→E002 / E001→E003: Rule 3 investigation gates; both downstream epics\n50\t  carry `gated_by: E001` with `gate_failure_impact` (action `rewrite` +\n51\t  fallback), and the direct E001→E003 edge is required so `gated_by` targets a\n52\t  direct dependency — not a redundant serialization.\n53\t- E002→E003: Rule 13 API producer → consuming implementation; the admin view\n54\t  builds against the report API. Justified.\n55\t- E002→E004, E003→E004: Rule 11 docs-authoring blocked by all Implementation\n56\t  epics. Complete coverage of the implementation set.\n57\t\n58\tFrontmatter `dependencies` match the diagram exactly in both directions;\n59\tarrow direction is dependency → dependent. No cycles, no invalid edges. No\n60\tonboarding/license epics exist, so Rules 7/8/10 parallelism is not in play.\n61\tCritical path (E001→E002→E003→E004, length 4) is at the top of the M-standard\n62\trange, but every edge is rule-mandated (investigation gate, producer→consumer,\n63\tdocs-last) — no avoidable serialization. Cross-check of epic content found no\n64\tuncaptured data/artifact dependency: the quota-figures dependency of E003 on\n65\tE002 is captured by the E002→E003 edge. No branch files exist; the summary\n66\trecords why (both bounded investigation outcomes change internal approach, not\n67\tepic existence), which is a legitimate gate-not-branch shape.\n68\t\n69\t### 3. Epic Boundaries (2/2)\n70\t\n71\tAll epics are single-component, single-team (RHOAI Dashboard). E002 (server\n72\tside) vs E003 (web UI) is a sub-system split within the Dashboard component —\n73\tallowed and correctly justified; it is producer/consumer layering, not\n74\tduplication (E002 owns the export endpoint and API; E003 owns the UI\n75\taffordance that invokes it — complementary layers, not the same work built\n76\ttwice). E004 is pure docs-authoring with no code/content work-product mixing.\n77\t`Distributed Workloads` is treated as passive with an explicit rationale and\n78\tits validation folded into reporting-epic ACs — no code change to it is\n79\tdescribed in the strategy, so no separate epic is warranted. All epics are\n80\twithin the size guideline; no overages, so no re-split triggers required.\n81\t\n82\t### 4. Type Correctness (2/2)\n83\t\n84\tE001 is a genuine Investigation: its outcome (contract stability, direct vs.\n85\tisolation-layer consumption) changes what E002/E003 do, and both depend on it.\n86\tE002/E003/E004 are Implementations producing concrete artifacts (report API +\n87\tCSV export, admin view, documentation topics). Gating metadata is complete and\n88\tcorrect: E002 and E003 both set `gated_by: RHAISTRAT-9018-E001` with\n89\t`gate_failure_impact` populated (action + fallback_approach); each `gated_by`\n90\ttarget appears in that epic's direct `dependencies`. E004 has no gate and\n91\tdepends only on implementations. E001 uses `investigation_signals`;\n92\tImplementation epics use `ai_signals` — correct signal sets per type.\n93\t\n94\t### 5. AI Implementability Scoring (2/2)\n95\t\n96\tSignal values verified against the type-appropriate rubrics and the strategy\n97\tcontent; rationales in the ai-signals files match the frontmatter values.\n98\t\n99\t- E001 (5-signal): `source_accessibility: 0` matches the rubric's exact\n100\t  condition (readable draft schema exists but the final answer doesn't —\n101\t  decision under review in another strategy); `cluster_hardware_dependence:\n102\t  -1` and `human_judgment_required: -1` correctly classify the cluster need\n103\t  and owner sign-off as peripheral, not gating.\n104\t- E002: `open_questions: -1` (consumption approach unresolved until the gate)\n105\t  and `external_dependency: -1` (data source owned by the in-flight metering\n106\t  strategy) match the rubric's -1 conditions; `architecture_claims: 1`